---
description: Compose components from smaller, focused sub-components
globs: "**/*.tsx"
---

Components should compose focused sub-components rather than implement large sections of UI directly.

Extract a sub-component when a section has its own:
- visual purpose
- interactions
- styling
- state
- meaningful name

Apply this recursively. Compound components should also be composed of focused sub-components.

Parent components should primarily orchestrate data flow and composition. Leaf components should own rendering details.

### One component per file

Each component should live in its **own file**, named after the component. Few exceptions:
- Tiny, tightly-coupled helper components used by a single parent (for example a small icon or internal sub-element) may stay in the parent's file if they have no standalone reuse or meaning.
- Module-scope constants and helpers that only one component needs belong in that component's file.